## 2. Electrical Schematic

### 2.1. Call Detector (AC Rectification & Filtering)

```
Riser Line (CA) ─────────>| [Diode 1N4007] |---+---------------+
                                                 |               |
                                                 | +             |
                                                 |-[Capacitor]   |----> IN+ (PC817 pin 1)
  Handset Pin 6 (GND) <──────────────────────────| (10 µF 25V)   |
  (Common System Ground)                         | -             |
                                                 +--------------> IN− (PC817 pin 2)
```

**PC817 output → ESP32:**

| PC817 | Connection |
|-------|------------|
| Pin 3 (collector) | **GPIO4** (INPUT_PULLUP) |
| Pin 4 (emitter) | GND |
| Pull-up (internal) | 3.3 V via ESP32 INPUT_PULLUP |

Logic: active **LOW** during a call (`inverted: true` in software).

**Filter components:**
- **1N4007** — clips negative half-waves, protects optocoupler LED.
- **10 µF 25 V** — smooths 50 Hz ripple into stable DC during ringing.

### 2.2. Automatic Door Release (PhotoMOS TLP172A)

A **PhotoMOS** solid-state relay bridges the handset lock contacts silently (no mechanical click).

```
       ESP32-C3                                     PhotoMOS (TLP172A)
     +-----------+                                      +---------+
     |   GPIO2   |---------[ Resistor 220 Ω ]--------->| 1 (IN+) |
     |           |                                      |         |
     |    GND    |------------------------------------->| 2 (IN−) |
     +-----------+                                      |         |
                                                        | 3 (OUT) |──> Handset Pin 9 (Lock)
                                                        |         |
                                                        | 4 (OUT) |──> Handset Pin 6 (Ground)
                                                        +---------+
```

> **Pin note:** GPIO5/GPIO6 are reserved for the onboard 0.42" OLED (I2C). PhotoMOS moved from GPIO5 → **GPIO2**.

### 2.3. Custom Ringback (Optional)

```
External +5 V ──> BC547 collector
GPIO18 ──[ 1 kΩ ]──> BC547 base
BC547 emitter ──> Freed CA terminal on Urmet PCB
```

### 2.4. OLED 0.42" Display (Onboard, SSD1306 72×40)

| Display | ESP32-C3 |
|---------|----------|
| VCC | 3.3 V |
| GND | GND |
| SDA | **GPIO5** |
| SCL | **GPIO6** |

Use **Software I2C** (U8g2 SW_I2C driver) — see generator spec §4 for snow/offset fix.

